-- title:
--   Transport of a fundamental domain along idelic Hilbert 90
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq L$ be number fields with $L/K$ finite Galois, and let $D$ be an idelic Galois descent datum for $L/K$: a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to the ring automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}_L$ which is compatible with the structure map $L \to \mathbb{A}_L$ and continuous in each automorphism; write $\tau \mapsto D.\mathrm{unitsAct}\,\tau$ for the induced automorphisms of $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$. Let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$, and let $\nu_{ZL}$ be a Haar measure on $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ for a Borel measurable structure. Assume given: a closed subgroup $A_K \le \mathbb{A}_L^\times$ whose members are exactly the images of elements of $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$ under the unit map of the base-change ring homomorphism $\beta$ of [`M4aHerbrand.GenuineDescent.genuineBaseChange K L`](def/M4aHerbrand_GenuineDescent.html#L87), with Haar measure $\mu_{A_K}$; a closed subgroup $N^1 \le \mathbb{A}_L^\times$ consisting exactly of the $z$ with idelic norm $1$, the idelic norm being the unit map of the algebra norm of $\mathbb{A}_L$ over $\mathbb{A}_K$ along $\beta$, with Haar measure $\mu_N$; and a constant $c_N > 0$ such that for every $g : \mathbb{A}_L^\times \to \mathbb{C}$ one has $\int_{N^1} g(n)\,d\mu_N = c_N \int_{q} g\big((D.\mathrm{unitsAct}\,\sigma)(q.\mathrm{out})\,(q.\mathrm{out})^{-1}\big)$, the second integral taken over the orbit quotient of $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ by $A_K$ with respect to [`HaarQuotient.measure νZL AK μAK`](def/HaarQuotient.html#L28), the pushforward under the quotient map of $\nu_{ZL}$ weighted by the density attached to $A_K$ and $\mu_{A_K}$, and $q.\mathrm{out}$ a chosen representative of $q$. Finally let $\Theta_1 \subseteq N^1$ be a fundamental domain, for $\mu_N$, of the subgroup of $N^1$ induced by the range of $w \mapsto \iota(\sigma(w)w^{-1})$, $\iota : L^\times \to \mathbb{A}_L^\times$. Put $F := \{q : (D.\mathrm{unitsAct}\,\sigma)(q.\mathrm{out})(q.\mathrm{out})^{-1} \in \Theta_1\}$, the membership being in the image of $\Theta_1$ in $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$. The conclusion has three parts: $F$ is null measurable for the quotient measure; for almost every class $q$ there is $w \in L^\times$ with the class of $\iota(w)\,q.\mathrm{out}$ in $F$; and for all $w, w' \in L^\times$ with $w^{-1}w'$ not in the image of $K^\times$, the intersection of $\{q : \text{class of } \iota(w)^{-1} q.\mathrm{out} \in F\}$ and $\{q : \text{class of } \iota(w')^{-1} q.\mathrm{out} \in F\}$ has quotient measure $0$.
--
--   This is the transport, along the idelic Hilbert 90 map $\bar z \mapsto \sigma(z)z^{-1}$ from $A_K \backslash \mathbb{A}_L^\times$ to the norm-one ideles, of a fundamental domain for the subgroup $\{\sigma(w)/w : w \in L^\times\}$ acting on $N^1$; disjointness is asserted only modulo $K^\times$, the kernel of $w \mapsto \sigma(w)/w$. It is used in [`NumberField.measure_fundamentalDomain_range_div_eq_mul_finrank_mul_div_of_ker_idelicNorm`](thm.html#NumberField.measure_fundamentalDomain_range_div_eq_mul_finrank_mul_div_of_ker_idelicNorm), which compares the volumes of the two fundamental domains.
